      "writtenOn": "2023-07-17T15:46:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I changed my mind about this again -- interrupting an entire replay is probably worse than dropping specific image draw calls for images that are too big. I don\u0027t think it makes sense to return a TextureProxy that we know can\u0027t be instantiated because the dimensions are too large, so I think this check makes sense here. I added a test trying to create promise images that are too large (exercising this code path) as well as empty (which we already catch).",
